 "read_me": {
  "Doors/deal": "Live list size divided by the deals that list produced in the window. Lower is better: fewer doors to work per closed deal.",
  "Lift": "County baseline doors/deal divided by the signal's doors/deal. 3.0 means three times sharper than pulling the whole county.",
  "Baseline": "The whole county unfiltered, counted the same way; the denominator every signal is judged against.",
  "Stack": "Records sitting on two distress lists at once. Stacks are distress plus distress; AI is never AND-stacked on distress.",
  "AI score": "DataSift Investor AI likelihood-to-sell score, 0-100, a PARALLEL pull alongside the distress lists.",
  "score-gated": "Live AI-scored supply counts are provisioned per account, so a local doors/deal cannot be computed in this view. The deals and coverage are this county's own data.",
  "Verify supply": "The row tripped the verify rule (v2.1 coverage-aware: verify reasons annotate (churn: doors/deal < 5; small: list < 250) without demoting; only judicial notice lists and churn artifacts (doors/deal < 1) force P3. Volume floors: P1 needs >=2% of county deal flow or >=25 deals, P2 >=1% or >=12 deals): demand is real, treat the efficiency as directional until you price the live list.",
  "Evidence A / B / C": "from this county's own sold deals / cross-market benchmark / single-market anchor (Knox + Blount TN AI measurement)",
  "Typical gross": "Median of AVM value minus purchase price on clean deals: acquisition spread, not net profit.",
  "Non-disclosure states": "Sale prices are not public there, so deal-dollar columns are omitted; doors/deal and lift never use dollars."
 },
